# Summary of changes for run e5d3f925-630f-4c4b-af3e-e3d8b22fd3a7
Delivered a clean, self-contained algebraic formalization of Australian Aboriginal kinship section/subsection systems.

The complete development lives in `Catalog/Applications/DreamtimeAlgebra/Defs.lean` (with `Catalog/Applications/DreamtimeAlgebra/Theorems.lean` reduced to a thin re-export). All earlier non-algebraic stubs were removed; there is no graph-reconstruction content, no `sorry`, and the theorems depend only on the standard axioms.

What is proved (one coherent story modelling each system as an elementary abelian 2-group):

1. `Section4` — a four-constructor finite type with an explicit `ZMod 2 × ZMod 2` bit-vector group law:
   - `DecidableEq` and `Fintype` (derived);
   - a full `AddCommGroup` instance (associative, commutative, identity, inverses), with every element self-inverse (`self_inverse`) and of order dividing 2 (`orderOf_dvd_two`);
   - `equivPair : Section4 ≃ ZMod 2 × ZMod 2` and the additive isomorphism `addEquivPair : Section4 ≃+ ZMod 2 × ZMod 2`.

2. `Subsection8` — an eight-constructor finite type with an explicit 3-bit `ZMod 2 × ZMod 2 × ZMod 2` group law:
   - `DecidableEq`, `Fintype`, full `AddCommGroup`, self-inverse, order dividing 2;
   - `equivBits` and the additive isomorphism `addEquivBits : Subsection8 ≃+ (ZMod 2)³`.

3. Marriage-rule algebra (translation by a fixed nonzero generator) for both systems:
   - `spouse_eq_transport`: the spouse map is exactly translation-by-(1,0…0) transported through the bit model (label independence);
   - `spouse_involutive` (involution) and `spouse_ne_self` (fixed-point-free exogamy), `spouse_ne_id`;
   - `spouse_equivariant`: `spouse (x + g) = spouse x + g`;
   - `map_spouse`: the spouse map commutes with the group isomorphism;
   - a child-class map `childClass x y = x + y + c` with `childClass_comm`, `childClass_equivariant_left`, and `childClass_spouse` showing every admissible couple `(x, spouse x)` produces children of a single fixed class independent of the parents' own sections.

General lemmas for elementary 2-groups (`translate_right_comm`, `translate_involutive`) are stated abstractly and instantiated for both n = 2 and n = 3. The file includes module documentation summarizing the model and results. Everything was verified to type-check end-to-end.
